@startuml

start

:Thermal management controller operates as state machine on hard real-time RTOS;
:Orchestrate multi-subsystem response to environmental sensor inputs；
:Continuously sample sensor fusion ring buffer protected by mutex;
:Aggregate calibrated data from;
fork
  :Temperature sensors;
fork again
  :Humidity sensors;
fork again
  :Light sensors;
fork again
  :Air quality sensors;
fork again
  :Occupancy sensors;
fork again
  :Contact sensors;
fork again
  :Smoke sensors;
end fork

fork
:Temperature or humidity > thresholds;
fork again
:Room is occupied;
fork again
:Windows are closed;
end fork

if (Detect primary fault condition?) then (yes)
  :Trigger concurrent mitigation sequence;
  fork
    :Command FADEC to activate via PWM-controlled liquid-cooling loops;
   fork
   :Air conditioner's cooling;
   fork again
   :Dehumidifier;
   end fork
  fork again
    :Monitor watchdog timer to ensure liveness;
  fork again
   :Lower-priority task manages air quality;
   if (CO2 critically high and no smoke detected?) then (yes)
    :Close smart curtains;
    :Activate air purifier;
    repeat
    :Poll air quality sensor with exponential backoff;
    repeat while(Concentrations return to safe range) is(no)
  else (no)
  end if
 end fork

else (no)
end if

:All sensor fusion and calibration routines execute in periodic RTOS tasks;
if (Out-of-range readings?) then (yes)
  :Engage redundant sensors;
  :Initiate controlled, state-managed cool-down path;
  :Maintain system integrity;
else (no)
end if

stop

@enduml
